{% from '_components/image' import Image %}

{#
  Overview:

  The Image component provides performant responsive images with minimal code.

  In most cases, you only need to think about the desired aspect ratio for the image
  and any sizes hints to help the browser determine the appropriate image size.

  The Image component will automatically auto-fill a range of image transforms
  to populate the srcset.

  Auto-filled transforms can be resource intensive. They work best with "Serverless
  Image Transforms", which is the recommended default for our Craft Site Starter.

  Serverless Image Transforms are generated by a lamda function only when the
  specific image URL is requested. This means that URLs in the srcset that are
  never requested are not generated.

  If you need to use named transforms, you can pass a string to the `transform` prop.

  Example:

    {{ Image({
      image: craft.assets.one(),
      sizes: {
        default: '50vw',
        sm: '25vw',
        md: '33vw',
      },
      ratio: 3/4,
    }) }}

  Output:

    <img
      class="w-full h-auto"
      src="image-420.webp"
      srcset="
        image-420.webp 420w,
        image-935.webp 935w,
        image-1450.webp 1450w,
        image-1965.webp 1965w,
        image-2480.webp 2480w"
        sizes="(min-width: 640px) 25vw, (min-width: 768px) 33vw, 50vw"
        ...additional attributes
      >
#}

<div class="container flex flex-col py-64 gap-32">
  {#
    Basic Example:
    Transforms and sizes are configured to work well with the .container class.
  #}
  <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Basic Example</h2>
  {{ Image({
    image: craft.assets.one(),
    ratio: 16/9,
  }) }}

  {#
    Custom Sizes:
    The keys of the sizes attribute correspond to the breakpoints in your Tailwind config.
    It uses a mobile first approach, default is the size used without a breakpoint.
  #}
  <div class="grid gap-16 grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 md:grid-cols-3">
    <div>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-16">Custom Sizes</h2>
      {{ Image({
        image: craft.assets.one(),
        sizes: {
          default: '50vw',
          sm: '25vw',
          md: '33vw',
        },
      }) }}
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-16">Custom Sizes and Aspect Ratio</h2>
      {{ Image({
        image: craft.assets.one(),
        sizes: {
          default: '50vw',
          sm: '25vw',
          md: '33vw',
        },
        ratio: 3/4,
      }) }}
    </div>
    <div>
      {#
        Named Transform:
        If you need to use a named transform, you can pass a string into the `transform` prop.
      #}
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-16">Named Transform</h2>
      {{ Image({
        image: craft.assets.one(),
        transform: 'exampleNamedTransform',
        sizes: {
          default: '50vw',
          sm: '25vw',
          md: '33vw',
        },
      }) }}
    </div>
    <div>
      {#
        Scalar Sizes
        This component supports custom transforms and scalar values for the sizes prop.
      #}
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-16">Scalar Sizes & Custom Transform</h2>
      {{ Image({
        image: craft.assets.one(),
        class: 'size-40',
        transformMinWidth: 40,
        transformMaxWidth: 80,
        transformAutofillCount: 0,
        ratio: 1/1,
        sizes: '40px',
      }) }}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

{#
  Full Bleed Image

  The defaults for the image component are configured to work well
  with a .container class.

  If you need to use a full bleed image, you can override the ranges
  of the auto-filled transforms.

  Example Output:

  <img
    class="w-full h-auto"
    src="image-800.webp"
    srcset="
      image-800.webp 800w,
      image-2000.webp 2000w,
      image-3200.webp 3200w
    "
    sizes="100vw"
    ...additional attributes
  >
#}

<div class="flex flex-col gap-32">
  <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Full Bleed Image</h2>
  {{ Image({
    image: craft.assets.one(),
    ratio: 16/9,
    transformMinWidth: 800,
    transformMaxWidth: 3200,
    transformAutofillCount: 1,
  }) }}
</div>
